# Exceptions for the Trivy scan (.github/trivy-scan.sh). Allowed only
#   a) for findings that were checked and provably cannot be exploited in AssetLotse, or
#   b) for a short time, when Debian has published the fix but snapshot.debian.org cannot deliver it yet,
#      and the image that is already published contains the same vulnerable version (the new release is
#      then not worse; the next security update brings the fix and the entry expires).
# Each entry needs, checked automatically:
#   - a reason on the line directly above, starting with "# reason:"
#   - an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD); after it the finding is reported again and checked anew
# Example:
#   # reason: affects only the XYZ parser, which AssetLotse never calls (checked 2026-10-25)
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2027-01-31

# reason: b) zlib1g fixed in 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1 (DSA-6613-1, 8 Nov 2026); the security import of 20261108T202647Z on snapshot.debian.org answers 404 for its package list, so the relock cannot fetch it. 2.3.0 has the same zlib. Remove with the next security update.
CVE-2026-27171 exp:2026-11-10
# reason: b) same zlib1g update as above (DSA-6613-1)
CVE-2026-76844 exp:2026-11-10
# reason: b) same zlib1g update as above (DSA-6613-1)
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-11-10
